1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,171
This video shows accounts and opportunities in the Omnichannel CRM:

2
00:00:05,171 --> 00:00:09,229
how contacts and deals are grouped under an account, how to add a

3
00:00:09,229 --> 00:00:13,400
deal and find it with search terms, what happens when an account is

4
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:15,400
deleted, and the CRM reports.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,456
A company has several people you talk to, and often more than one deal in progress.

6
00:00:25,456 --> 00:00:29,380
Looking at each person alone hides the whole relationship.

7
00:00:30,130 --> 00:00:32,847
An account is the company or household.

8
00:00:32,847 --> 00:00:38,340
Its contacts and its opportunities hang under it, so you see everything in one place.

9
00:00:39,090 --> 00:00:40,925
An opportunity is a deal.

10
00:00:40,925 --> 00:00:44,951
It has a stage, an amount, a close date and a primary contact,

11
00:00:44,951 --> 00:00:47,200
and it can belong to an account.

12
00:00:51,384 --> 00:00:54,150
Open Interaction Center, Accounts.

13
00:00:54,150 --> 00:00:56,156
Each row is an account.

14
00:00:56,156 --> 00:00:59,544
Click List Items on a row to open its page.

15
00:01:00,006 --> 00:01:06,094
The account's page lists its contacts and its opportunities, with the usual search and filters.

16
00:01:06,094 --> 00:01:08,866
Edit Account changes the account itself.

17
00:01:09,318 --> 00:01:13,791
List Activities shows the activities of every contact in the account, so a

18
00:01:13,791 --> 00:01:17,258
supervisor sees the whole conversation with the company.

19
00:01:21,432 --> 00:01:25,449
A contact joins an account with the Account picker on its editor.

20
00:01:25,449 --> 00:01:28,732
Open a contact and choose the account from the list.

21
00:01:30,382 --> 00:01:32,805
Opportunities have the same picker.

22
00:01:32,805 --> 00:01:37,592
Every contact and opportunity type can join an account without extra setup.

23
00:01:37,592 --> 00:01:39,601
Leads never join an account:

24
00:01:39,601 --> 00:01:42,142
they get one when they are converted.

25
00:01:46,336 --> 00:01:49,178
Open Interaction Center, Opportunities.

26
00:01:49,178 --> 00:01:54,546
The list shows the open opportunities, with the account, the stage, the amount,

27
00:01:54,546 --> 00:01:57,136
the probability and the close date.

28
00:01:57,587 --> 00:01:59,164
Search with terms.

29
00:01:59,164 --> 00:02:04,484
Stage finds a stage by name, Closed finds closed or open opportunities, Won

30
00:02:04,484 --> 00:02:09,607
finds the ones that were won, and Account finds the deals of an account.

31
00:02:13,830 --> 00:02:15,982
Click New Sales Opportunity.

32
00:02:15,982 --> 00:02:21,490
Pick the Account, give the deal a title, and enter the Amount and the Close date.

33
00:02:22,278 --> 00:02:25,657
The Primary contact picker lists your contact types.

34
00:02:25,657 --> 00:02:30,027
The Stage decides whether the opportunity is open, won or lost, and a

35
00:02:30,027 --> 00:02:33,698
new opportunity starts with the probability of its stage.

36
00:02:34,151 --> 00:02:38,646
The Opportunity owner, the Lead source and the Campaign are optional.

37
00:02:38,646 --> 00:02:42,961
Publish the opportunity, and it is on the list and in the account.

38
00:02:47,166 --> 00:02:50,899
Use Actions, Delete on an account row to remove it.

39
00:02:50,899 --> 00:02:57,056
Deleting an account leaves its contacts and opportunities in place, outside any account.

40
00:02:57,506 --> 00:03:01,708
The contacts are still on the Contacts list, and the opportunity is still

41
00:03:01,708 --> 00:03:04,686
on the Opportunities list, now without an account.

42
00:03:08,886 --> 00:03:15,965
Three reports appear under Reports, CRM and Campaigns, and need the View Omnichannel reports permission.

43
00:03:15,965 --> 00:03:18,346
Each is filtered by date range.

44
00:03:19,096 --> 00:03:23,517
The Lead funnel shows the leads created in the period by their current

45
00:03:23,517 --> 00:03:25,785
status, with the share converted.

46
00:03:25,785 --> 00:03:31,019
Lead conversion by source and list shows leads, conversions, the conversion rate and

47
00:03:31,019 --> 00:03:32,996
the average time to convert.

48
00:03:33,746 --> 00:03:38,674
The Opportunity pipeline shows the open opportunities by stage with their amount and

49
00:03:38,674 --> 00:03:42,506
weighted amount, and the win rate of those closed in the period.

50
00:03:46,706 --> 00:03:51,526
See every person and every deal of a company on one page.

51
00:03:52,276 --> 00:03:57,026
Review the whole conversation with a company, across all its contacts.

52
00:03:57,776 --> 00:04:02,746
Track deals by stage and amount, and see what is closing this month.

53
00:04:03,496 --> 00:04:08,516
Report on the pipeline and on how well each lead source converts.

54
00:04:10,516 --> 00:04:14,403
Group the contacts and the deals of a company under one account, follow

55
00:04:14,403 --> 00:04:18,390
every deal through its stages, and read the pipeline and the lead sources

56
00:04:18,390 --> 00:04:21,519
in the reports, so you always know what is closing next.

57
00:04:21,519 --> 00:04:25,354
The user manual and the technical guide are linked in the description.

58
00:04:25,354 --> 00:04:26,666
Thanks for watching.

